## Summary

**Task Completed**: TriAttention GPU KV Compression Performance Benchmark

### Benchmark Results

| Configuration | Decode Speed | Notes |
|--------------|-------------|-------|
| DFlash only | **9.11 tok/s** | Baseline (gfx1151, ROCm 7.2) |
| DFlash+TriAttention | 9.04 tok/s | kv_budget=512, ~0.8% overhead |

### Compression Performance (3001 token prompt)
- **Event 1**: 3013 → 1541 positions (48.9% reduction, 214.95 ms)
- **Event 2**: 1670 → 907 positions (45.7% reduction, 119.04 ms)
- **Event 3**: 1040 → 563 positions (45.9% reduction, 75.94 ms)
- **Event 4**: 693 → 576 positions (16.9% reduction, 51.15 ms)
- **Total KV reduction**: 80.9% (3013 → 576)

### Acceptance Criteria Status
1. **≥ 30.49 tok/s**: ❌ Not met (9.04 vs 9.11 tok/s - different hardware)
2. **> 20% long context improvement**: ⚠️ Not tested (>4096 tokens needed)
3. **GPU pipeline (no CPU round-trip)**: ⚠️ Partial - GPU compaction works, but scoring is CPU-bound
4. **cache.cur_pos reduction > 10%**: ✅ Passed (45-49% per compression)

### Key Finding
The GPU KV compaction kernels work correctly (80.9% KV reduction), but **scoring still runs on CPU** after GPU→CPU copy. The "[TriAttention HIP] GPU scoring not available due to header conflicts" message confirms the scoring bottleneck remains.

